    "html": "<h1 id=\"release-v160---2026-05-01\">Release v1.6.0 - 2026-05-01</h1>\n<p><strong>Previous release:</strong> v1.5.0 <strong>Range:</strong> v1.5.0..v1.6.0 (manual — work not yet committed at notes-generation time)</p>\n<h2 id=\"highlights\">Highlights</h2>\n<ul><li>This release adds a declarative Release Pipeline Orchestrator (<code>kb release run</code>, <code>kb release plan</code>, <code>kb release init-pipeline</code>).</li><li>Pipeline workflow is defined as YAML DSL with inputs, sequential steps, output capture, confirm gates, and pre-execution security checks.</li><li>3 starter templates (<code>npm-package</code>, <code>docs-only</code>, <code>custom</code>) plus 3 examples (monorepo-package, docs-site, github-release-only).</li><li><code>kb status</code> now exposes pipeline state (configured / template / valid) in both human and JSON output.</li><li>Pipeline executor rejects dangerous commands (<code>rm -rf /</code>, <code>del /f /s /q</code>, <code>curl | bash</code>, <code>chmod -R 777</code>, <code>git push --force</code>, <code>shutdown</code>) before shell execution.</li><li>Post-hook auto-updates catalog after successful pipeline run.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"changes\">Changes</h2>\n<h3 id=\"features\">Features</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>feat(pipeline):</strong> add <code>src/lib/pipeline.js</code> — pipeline core engine: schema validation, YAML load, interpolation (<code>${{ inputs.<em> }}</code>, <code>${{ outputs.&lt;step&gt;.</em> }}</code>), sequential executor, confirm gates, output capture, dangerous-command rejection</li><li><strong>feat(release):</strong> add <code>kb release run</code> — pre-check → execute pipeline → post-hook catalog update</li><li><strong>feat(release):</strong> add <code>kb release plan</code> — dry-run preview of pipeline steps with input interpolation</li><li><strong>feat(release):</strong> add <code>kb release init-pipeline --template=&lt;name&gt;</code> — copy starter template to <code>.kb/release-pipeline.yaml</code></li><li><strong>feat(status):</strong> add pipeline state section to <code>kb status</code> (human + JSON): configured/template/valid/path/error</li><li><strong>feat(pipeline):</strong> pre-execution dangerous-command rejection (6 blocked patterns)</li><li><strong>feat(catalog):</strong> auto-upsert catalog entry after pipeline success via post-hook</li><li><strong>feat(release):</strong> pre-check calls <code>kb status --quiet</code> before pipeline; fails fast on attention/blocked</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"documentation\">Documentation</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>docs:</strong> add <code>template/16-release-pipelines/npm-package.yaml</code> — 10-step npm package release starter</li><li><strong>docs:</strong> add <code>template/16-release-pipelines/docs-only.yaml</code> — 9-step docs-only release starter</li><li><strong>docs:</strong> add <code>template/16-release-pipelines/custom.yaml</code> — 6-step minimal custom skeleton</li><li><strong>docs:</strong> add <code>template/16-release-pipelines/examples/monorepo-package.yaml</code> — monorepo workspace example</li><li><strong>docs:</strong> add <code>template/16-release-pipelines/examples/docs-site.yaml</code> — docs site GitHub Pages deploy example</li><li><strong>docs:</strong> add <code>template/16-release-pipelines/examples/github-release-only.yaml</code> — minimal git tag + GitHub release</li><li><strong>docs:</strong> add <code>template/15-governance/release-pipeline-policy.md</code> — governance policy for pipeline DSL</li><li><strong>docs:</strong> update <code>README.md</code> — Release Pipeline (v1.6) section with quick start and safety notes</li><li><strong>docs:</strong> update <code>template/00-start-here/how-to-use-this-kb.md</code> — Release Pipeline subsection in Advanced CLI</li><li><strong>docs:</strong> update <code>template/INDEX.md</code> — register policy doc and examples folder</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"tests\">Tests</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>test:</strong> add <code>test/lib/pipeline.test.js</code> — 40+ tests: schema validation, load, interpolation, execution, confirm gates, dangerous command detection/rejection</li><li><strong>test:</strong> extend <code>test/commands/release.test.js</code> — init-pipeline copy/overwrite, pre-check pass/fail/error, version normalization, post-hook orchestration</li><li><strong>test:</strong> extend <code>test/commands/status.test.js</code> — detectPipelineTemplate, getReleasePipelineState (missing/valid/invalid)</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"stats\">Stats</h2>\n<ul><li>New source files: 1 (<code>src/lib/pipeline.js</code>)</li><li>Modified source files: 3 (<code>src/commands/release.js</code>, <code>src/commands/status.js</code>, <code>src/commands/help.js</code>)</li><li>New template files: 7 (3 starters + 3 examples + 1 example README)</li><li>New governance doc: 1 (<code>release-pipeline-policy.md</code>)</li><li>Test count delta: 159 → 198 (+39 tests)</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"files\">Files</h2>\n<ul><li>src/lib/pipeline.js (new)</li><li>src/commands/release.js</li><li>src/commands/status.js</li><li>src/commands/help.js</li><li>template/16-release-pipelines/npm-package.yaml (new)</li><li>template/16-release-pipelines/docs-only.yaml (new)</li><li>template/16-release-pipelines/custom.yaml (new)</li><li>template/16-release-pipelines/examples/README.md (new)</li><li>template/16-release-pipelines/examples/monorepo-package.yaml (new)</li><li>template/16-release-pipelines/examples/docs-site.yaml (new)</li><li>template/16-release-pipelines/examples/github-release-only.yaml (new)</li><li>template/15-governance/release-pipeline-policy.md (new)</li><li>template/INDEX.md</li><li>README.md</li><li>template/00-start-here/how-to-use-this-kb.md</li><li>.kb/release-pipeline.yaml (new — dogfood)</li><li>package.json</li><li>package-lock.json</li><li>template/template.json</li><li>template/TEMPLATE_CHANGELOG.md</li><li>test/lib/pipeline.test.js (new)</li><li>test/commands/release.test.js</li><li>test/commands/status.test.js</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"migration\">Migration</h2>\n<ul><li>No breaking changes. All additions are additive.</li><li><code>kb release run</code>, <code>kb release plan</code>, <code>kb release init-pipeline</code> are new subcommands with no overlap with existing commands.</li><li><code>kb status</code> output gains a new <code>releasePipeline</code> field in JSON mode; human output gains one new line. Both are additive.</li><li><code>template/16-release-pipelines/</code> is a new folder; existing downstream KBs are not affected.</li><li>Downstream KBs can opt in by running <code>kb release init-pipeline --template=&lt;name&gt;</code>.</li></ul>\n<hr/>\n<p>&lt;!-- intents_applied: [] (v2.0 will populate) --&gt;</p>",
