    "html": "<h1 id=\"release-v140-2026-05-01\">Release v1.4.0 — 2026-05-01</h1>\n<blockquote>Manual Phase 0 dogfood. Heuristic per <code>notes/upgrade-v1.5-catalog-release-notes-plan.md</code> §2.3. Pipeline applied by hand: detect previous via catalog (<code>v1.3.0</code>) → <code>git log v1.3.0..v1.4.0</code> → conventional-commit prefix grouping → markdown.</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Previous release:</strong> v1.3.0 (f8b4e58) <strong>Range:</strong> v1.3.0..v1.4.0 (574f8b5)</p>\n<h2 id=\"highlights\">Highlights</h2>\n<p>The impact engine ships. KB now turns a code change into a ranked list of affected docs via an in-memory dependency graph (<code>graphology</code>). New commands: <code>kb impact</code>, <code>kb verify</code>, <code>kb baseline</code>, <code>kb scan --recursive</code>. New doctor checks for <code>related_strong</code> cycles and missing <code>last_verified_commit</code>. New governance doc <code>template/15-governance/impact-policy.md</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"changes\">Changes</h2>\n<h3 id=\"features\">Features</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>feat(impact):</strong> recursive expansion + cycle detection — <code>kb scan --recursive [--depth=N]</code> writes <code>transitive_impacted[]</code> + <code>transitive_depth</code> into <code>impact.json</code> (additive, P3 backward-compat); <code>kb status</code> shows recursive impact line; <code>kb doctor</code> adds <code>related-strong-cycle</code> WARN check.</li><li><strong>feat:</strong> add configuration management and impact graph functionality — <code>src/lib/config.js</code> defaults loader, <code>src/lib/impact-graph.js</code> with BFS-limited traversal, <code>kb impact &lt;target&gt; [--depth=N] [--json]</code> with promote_hint, <code>kb verify &lt;doc&gt; | --all</code> with atomic last_verified_commit fill, <code>kb baseline show | set &lt;sha&gt; | --to-head</code>, doctor INFO <code>related-legacy-field</code> + WARN <code>related-strong-weak-conflict</code> + WARN <code>last-verified-commit-missing</code>. Template additions: <code>15-governance/related-semantic.md</code> (D14), <code>15-governance/metadata-schema.md</code> Field Rules + Validation Checklist.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"chore\">Chore</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>chore:</strong> advance baseline to v1.3.0 (f8b4e58) — <code>template/00-start-here/repository-revision-state.md</code> baseline anchor advanced after v1.3.0 release.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"docs\">Docs</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>docs(release):</strong> generate v1.4.0 changelog entry — <code>template/TEMPLATE_CHANGELOG.md</code> v1.4.0 section.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"stats\">Stats</h2>\n<ul><li>Commits in range: 4</li><li>Docs changed (<code>template/**</code>): 10</li><li>Code changed (<code>src/<strong></code>, <code>bin/</strong></code>, <code>tools/<strong></code>, <code>scripts/</strong></code>): 10</li><li>KB self-edits filtered: n/a (release session)</li><li>Intents applied: 0 (intent layer ships in v2.0)</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"files-added-changed-top-level\">Files Added / Changed (top level)</h2>\n<ul><li><code>package.json</code> (1.3.0 → 1.4.0; +graphology, +graphology-traversal)</li><li><code>src/lib/config.js</code> (new)</li><li><code>src/lib/impact-graph.js</code> (new, ~300 LOC)</li><li><code>src/commands/impact.js</code> (new)</li><li><code>src/commands/verify.js</code> (new)</li><li><code>src/commands/baseline.js</code> (new)</li><li><code>src/commands/scan.js</code> (--recursive flag)</li><li><code>src/commands/status.js</code> (recursive impact line)</li><li><code>src/commands/doctor.js</code> (3 new checks)</li><li><code>template/15-governance/impact-policy.md</code> (new)</li><li><code>template/15-governance/related-semantic.md</code> (new)</li><li><code>template/15-governance/metadata-schema.md</code> (Field Rules + Validation Checklist)</li><li><code>template/TEMPLATE_CHANGELOG.md</code> (v1.4.0 entry)</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"migration\">Migration</h2>\n<ul><li>Backward compatible (P3 additive). <code>impact.json</code> gains optional <code>transitive_impacted[]</code> + <code>transitive_depth</code> only when <code>kb scan --recursive</code> was the writer; readers ignore unknown fields per template-versioning-policy.</li></ul>\n<hr/>\n<p>&lt;!-- intents_applied: [] (v2.0 will populate) --&gt;</p>",
